-- INSIGHT: the tropical valuation profile is a *lax* semiring morphism: it is an exact
--   morphism for ⊗ (products) and only a lax morphism for ⊕ (sums / convolutions), with the
--   slack measured by cancellation among same-valuation terms (the Newton-polygon "collinear"
--   case).  This mirrors the general fact that tropicalization is a morphism precisely on the
--   "generic" (unique-minimizer) locus.
-- FAILURE ANALYSIS: an exact equality `val(cauchy) = inf(...)` is FALSE in general — e.g. two
--   terms of equal minimal valuation can cancel `p`-adically, raising the valuation of the
--   sum strictly above the min.  Hence only the ≥ direction is a theorem; the equality is a
--   *generic* statement requiring a unique-minimizer hypothesis (recorded in
--   FUTURE_DIRECTIONS.md).
-- INSIGHT: connecting to `CombinatorialSpecies.binConv`, the binomial-coefficient valuations
--   `val p (C(n,i))` are exactly Kummer's carry counts in base `p`; the species-product
--   tropical law therefore *sees* the base-`p` carry structure of the index `n`.

end

end SpeciesValuationProfile
